Package: rtfreporter
Type: Package
Title: Clinical RTF Reporting Toolkit for Tables, Listings and Figures
Version: 0.8.2.9100
Authors@R: c(
    person(given  = "Yoichi",
           family = "Masui",
           email  = "ichi.r.pro@gmail.com",
           role   = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Shoichi", "Fujita", email = "shoichi.fujita@takeda.com", role = "cre"))
Description: A standalone toolkit for generating Rich Text Format (RTF)
    reports used in clinical trial deliverables -- Tables, Listings and
    Figures (TFLs). Provides a functional, pipe-friendly API to compose
    documents with multi-section headers and footers, multi-row column
    headers including spanning groups, per-column formatting, automatic
    page-number fields, embedded PNG/JPEG/EMF figures, and clinical-style
    borders. Tables can also be made from an analysis results dataset
    (ARD, as built by 'cards' and 'cardx') with a plan of small verbs:
    which keys are columns and rows, how the statistics are formatted, and
    how the table is paged. Requires only packages that ship with R.
